  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Ketanserin, the closest structural analog sharing the 4-fluorophenyl ketone, piperidine, and cyclic-urea motif, has absolute oral bioavailability of 49.3 ± 18.0% (range 27–69%) by AUC and about 60% by F = 1 − E in fasted subjects, both above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C19"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sertindole, combining piperidine, fluorophenyl, and cyclic-urea heterocycle, has oral bioavailability approximately 74–75%; L2 records show tablet relative bioavailability about 75% and tablet-to-solution near unity.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C08", "C11", "C20", "C22", "C31"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Trazodone, sharing a propyl-linked azole-fused cyclic amide and aryl piperazine/piperidine-like scaffold, has absolute oral bioavailability 63–91% across fasted and fed groups; crossover records report 63–65%.",
      "card_ids": ["C02", "C05", "C10", "C15", "C03", "C24", "C25", "C30", "C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Maraviroc, a piperidine-containing oral drug, has population F estimates of 0.24 at 100 mg fasted and 33% at 600 mg, both above threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C16", "C21", "C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Setipiprant, PBA, cerivastatin, BAL27862, and encainide provide additional transferable oral-bioavailability evidence of at least 50–80% (or 0.52 in one poor-metabolizer cirrhosis patient), all above threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C14", "C23", "C26", "C01", "C28", "C06", "C13", "C04", "C09", "C12", "C18", "C27", "C33"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 record for DMP (M01), which shares the benzimidazolone-piperidine-propyl fragment with the query, reports Papp A→B >1×10^-5 cm/s, indicating high permeability and supporting the absorption component.",
      "card_ids": ["C49"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility/dissolution records for DMP (5.898 mg/mL in Tween 20; 100% release from SEDDS in 4 h) are formulation-specific but consistent with adequate solubility/dissolution.",
      "card_ids": ["C51", "C52"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 risperidone liquisolid dissolution records (C46–C48, C50, C53–C57) concern M02 and are not applicable to the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C46", "C47", "C48", "C50", "C53", "C54", "C55", "C56", "C57"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C49", "C51", "C52"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the exact query molecule (benperidol-like butyrophenone/piperidine benzimidazolone).",
    "Query-specific permeability, solubility, and dissolution data are absent; L4 records are for M01/M02, not the query.",
    "Formulation and prandial state for the query are unspecified, while several supporting records are formulation- or prandial-state-dependent.",
    "First-pass metabolism and clearance for the query are not measured; the physicochemical prior flags a permeability liability due to complete ionization and low logD, but this is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
    "Structural transfer from analogs is qualitative; no exact structural match is present in the record set."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because multiple transferable L1 absolute-oral-bioavailability records for close structural analogs — especially ketanserin (49–60%), sertindole (~74–75%), trazodone (63–91%), and maraviroc (24–33%) — meet or exceed the threshold, and no affirmative evidence supports F < 20%. L4 adds supportive but indirect absorption evidence: Caco-2 Papp >1×10^-5 cm/s for a compound sharing the benzimidazolone-piperidine-propyl fragment, plus favorable solubility/dissolution records for that compound. Confidence remains moderate because the L4 permeability/solubility data are not query-specific and the physicochemical prior still flags an absorption liability."
}

